<title>HONG KONG: New World says mulling CB for new company.</title>
<headline>New World says mulling CB for new company.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>New World Development Co Ltd said on Monday it was investigating with professional advisers the possibility of a proposed issue of bonds convertible into shares of a new company.</p>
<p>The new company would hold a portfolio of certain properties of the group in China, the statement said.</p>
<p>The company director Henry Cheng said &quot;no definite decision has been made by the company in relation to the size, timing and terms of the proposed bond issue&quot;.</p>
<p>New World shares were unchanged at HK$39.40 per share in early trade. -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
